Moreover, even if no error is returned in the response, there are multiple conditions that seem to bypass authentication based on user rights. An attacker might be able to manipulate these values to get unauthorised access or perform actions they shouldn't be allowed to do.

The function appears to store and forward sensitive information (user notes) without encryption. This could potentially lead to data leakage if the system is compromised. 

All of these issues highlight a significant security risk, with potential for severe exploitation. As such, it should be considered one of the most critical functions in this application, and any fixes or improvements should take into account all possible attack vectors.
