This can be mitigated by using prepared statements with placeholders for values that will change, such as module codes in this case. This approach ensures that user input is treated as literal string and not part of the actual query structure. 

Moreover, this function does not provide any protection against SQL injection attacks because the database operation is performed outside of a SQLAlchemy session or similar ORM-type context. Properly securing database operations with these types of contexts would ensure that data access is properly controlled and authorized.
