Secondly, the `db_connect()` function without any additional security measures like SSL or authentication is creating a direct connection to the database which makes it susceptible for eavesdropping and Man in the Middle attacks. 
  
Finally, if an attacker can execute SQL commands via this code, they could manipulate the 'name' parameter to run unauthorized commands on the server (which may result into complete system takeover). This could be a high confidence level of vulnerability due to direct user-supplied inputs being used in such a manner.
