<analysis>
This function may present a SQL injection vulnerability. The reason is the user input (search query) is directly concatenated into an SQL statement without any sanitisation or parameterization, which can be exploited by malicious users to perform SQL injections and execute arbitrary SQL commands. 

For instance, if an attacker were to provide a search term such as "admin' --", the resulting query would become: 
"select * from systems where lower(name) = 'admin'" -- which will delete all records from the systems table.

Moreover, it appears that the function is converting user input into lowercase before running a comparison in SQL. This might prevent case-sensitive matches and could lead to information disclosure if there are non-standardized casing differences. 

The returned results formatting can be improved by checking for empty or None values, which may cause errors when trying to print them out. The function also lacks exception handling which might not be desirable in a production environment.
</analysis>

