6. Regular Code Review and Security Testing: 
   Perform regular code reviews to spot possible security loopholes or vulnerabilities. Also, perform penetration testing regularly if possible. This can help identify potential attack vectors.

Remember that no matter how robust your application is, it's just as vulnerable when being used by malicious users. Always educate and inform your users about the risks associated with using your services. 

