1. There's a SQL Injection potential because the input from user (username) is directly incorporated into an SQL query without any sanitization, which could lead to unauthorized data access or manipulation if there are more complex queries being constructed elsewhere in the code. This vulnerability has been labelled as High Confidence CWE-89.
