The function _bson_iter_next_internal takes as parameters (bson_iter_t *iter, uint32_t next_keylen, const char **key, uint32_t *bson_type, bool *unsupported). The first parameter is a pointer to the iterator. In this function, there are no checks or validations that prevent reading beyond the end of the input BSON document. This could lead to buffer overflow vulnerability when it reads beyond allocated memory space leading to possible code execution and system compromise.
</analysis>

