1. Invalid Flag Value Check Failure (CWE-843): This issue arises due to a lack of validation for certain flag values in the function `do_get_mempolicy`. The flags parameter is checked against a bitwise AND operation with a long integer literal that represents specific flag bits (MPOL_F_NODE, MPOL_F_ADDR, MPOL_F_MEMS_ALLOWED). If an attacker manages to pass in a value for the flags parameter which isn't one of these predefined bit flags, it will bypass our validation and lead to unpredictable behavior.
   
2. Exposed Internal Data Structure (CWE-563): The function `do_get_mempolicy` directly exposes an internal data structure through the policy parameter without any additional checks or access controls. If an attacker has knowledge of how this function operates, they could manipulate the value of the policy to perform unwanted actions in the operating system kernel.

Both vulnerabilities have high confidence level. 

