However, without more context (like knowing what kind of data is supposed to be in this function), this can only be considered a "suspected" vulnerability with medium confidence level. 

Also, the R_NEW0() call could potentially allocate memory that's never freed, which would be an unprotected resource leak if it were not properly handled elsewhere in the codebase and not deallocated when no longer required. This is a moderate severity issue, with medium confidence level. 

</analysis>

