    - CWE-269: Unsafe Cryptographic Algorithm (Medium Confidence)

These vulnerabilities can potentially lead to unintended behaviors or security issues if not properly handled. They are rated as low confidence because they don't seem to be particularly exploitable in their current form, but it's always a good idea to consider them when assessing the overall security posture of an application.


