2. Incomplete Check for Line Termination - The code checks for line terminators ('\r' or '\n') but does not handle the case where these characters are found within a larger string of data. For example, in the input "hello\rworld", it would process "hello" as a line and "\rworld" without checking if it is also a valid line termination. This could allow for false positives or negatives depending on usage. Confidence level: Medium. CWE-835: Incomplete Check for Security-relevant Input During Web Page Generation.
3. Lack of Escape Handling - The code treats any character as data to be emitted and processed (in the switch statement), without checking if it needs escaping or not. This can lead to unintended behavior, such as script execution or command injection depending on usage. Confidence level: High. CWE-707: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection') 
</analysis>

