   The function catches exceptions and returns `False` in case of errors. While this prevents the application from crashing, it might hide important security-related issues that should be addressed more explicitly. Depending on how these functions are used elsewhere in the codebase, this could potentially allow an attacker to infer information about the system's internal state.

