This is a classic example of CWE-89: SQL Injection, where user input is directly incorporated into an SQL query without proper sanitization or use of prepared statements.

The severity of this vulnerability is high because it can lead to unauthorized access to data, data corruption, and potentially full system compromise depending on the database configuration and privileges.
