     if (w > MAX_DIMENSION || h > MAX_DIMENSION || maxval > MAX_MAXVAL) {
       ERREXIT(cinfo, JERR_BAD_PPM_FORMAT);
     }
     ```

2. **Integer Overflow Prevention**:
   - Use safe integer arithmetic functions to prevent overflow during buffer size calculations:
     ```c
     #include <stdint.h>
     #include <limits.h>

     size_t safe_mult(size_t a, size_t b) {
       if (a > 0 && b > 0 && UINT_MAX / a < b) {
         ERREXIT(cinfo, JERR_BAD_PPM_FORMAT); // Handle overflow
       }
       return a * b;
