4. CWE-787 (Out-of-bounds Write) - Medium Confidence (related to potential bounds checking issues with `copy_from_user`)
5. CWE-676 (Use of Potentially Dangerous Function) - Medium Confidence (use of `goto` for loop control and error handling)
6. CWE-362 (Race Condition) - Low Confidence (potential race conditions in spinlock usage)
7. CWE-416 (Use After Free) - Low Confidence (potential resource leaks in error paths)

The vulnerabilities vary in severity, with some posing more significant risks than others depending on the specific system configuration and attacker capabilities.

